{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794778923,"nonce":"NJJ/Nk9x+quUeI6Cwjtn6C5Vx3g=","message":"Clip paths on rows, local: 5108c9f0 'a path clip follows the rows of the node that moves it'.\n\n- Primitives carry the depth from which their path clip follows rows in clip_shape.y (set from CompositeBindingMeta::ambient_path, the path pointer in force when a bound node began, compared like ambient_clip). The SDF/notch/shadow fragment shaders take the pixel back through those rows, with the polygon's four AA samples along screen steps mapped back, so a turn is allowed. The CPU twin (CPU rows backend, layered overlays) copies the contour block and moves its points.\n- same_clip: the unbounded default clip rect matches no ambient clip; before, every unclipped primitive counted as having its own clip and refused any turn.\n- clip-path is no longer a scroll-row blocker.\n- Harness: 'css keyframes, spinners' (3 cn spinners) and 'scroll a list of spinners' in ON_ROWS, every frame on rows and matching the full paint at 2 levels on the table and the CPU rows. Before, the spinner scene was full rows:declined 12/12.\n\ncn_demo census: page on rows: true, no blockers left.\n\nThe page still did not scroll on rows: the layout epoch moved every frame (hover restyle base reset + incidental align-self ping-pong), so scroll_rows_tree_changed read it stale. Fixed in 02ed7549, issue 4ef35f2 (closed). Headless cn_demo scrolling 36 px/frame over 90 frames: full 90 at render 4.99 ms median, session 0.70 ms -\u003e 80 rows applied / 7 full / 3 declined, render 0.42 ms median (p90 4.92), session 0.13 ms.\n\nFollow-ups filed: e627d83 (a hover change restyles every element with state rules), 8346999 (layer-effect pass does not move a following path clip). Not yet chased: the 7 full and 3 declined scroll frames, and the moving label glyph edge inside a scrolled container.","files":null}]}